{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a multimodal model integrating ResNet50 image features with an optimized RNA-only baseline (scvi_n200 encoder, avgpool aggregation), achieving validation accuracy of 0.6315 (vs 0.653 for RNA-only). The lower accuracy suggests multimodal integration may not improve performance in this configuration, though the small effect size and lack of direct comparisons with alternative fusion strategies leave uncertainty. Initial observations indicate potential challenges in combining RNA and image modalities without further optimization."
}

